    "summary": "Woman&#039;s head-cover (waqaya or lihaf) made of purple cotton with a border sewn around the edges of orange wool fabric with floral patterns and golden threads. Worn over the head and fastened with a chin-strap made of black wool embellished with plaited metallic trim (seem or talli). Worn over a contrasting dress (dishdasha, 2011,6003.36) and baggy trousers (2011,6003.37). Can also be worn under a second head covering (kanga or leso, and two different head coverings (2011,6003.39).",
